  "headline_sentences": [
    "Raising the auto-flag threshold from 0.5 to 0.95 cuts false fraud alerts from 26.9 to 1.1 per 10,000 transactions (96.1% fewer, 95% CI 92.7% to 98.7%). The review queue plays no part in that cut: the same threshold with no review raises the identical 59 alerts.",
    "What the review band adds is on the miss side. The 0.95 threshold alone clears 22 of 75 frauds without a human look; sending the 0.05 to 0.95 middle to review (709 per 10,000) cuts that to 6, against 12 under the 0.5 default (paired bootstrap, 2 to 11 fewer than 0.5). Whether reviewers catch the 16 frauds in the queue is not measured.",
    "Counting the queue, 719.4 transactions per 10,000 are flagged or queued against 37.9 under the 0.5 default, and 707.3 of them are legitimate: most of the false-alert cut is legitimate traffic moved from alert to review, not removed.",
    "By value, the band surfaces 97.2% of the fold's fraud amount (auto-flag plus review, 95% CI 89.5% to 99.95%), exactly the set a single 0.05 threshold flags; the 0.5 default surfaces 66.4% (paired difference 95% CI 4.4 to 61.1 points)."
  ],
  "resume_sentences": [
    "Raising the auto-flag threshold from 0.5 to 0.95 cut false fraud alerts 96% (26.9 to 1.1 per 10,000 transactions, 95% CI 93% to 99%) on a temporal holdout of 56,961 real card transactions; a review band on the 0.05 to 0.95 middle routed to a human 16 of the 22 frauds that threshold alone auto-clears, at 709 reviews per 10,000.",
    "Split the 97.2% of fraud value that a single 0.05 threshold surfaces (95% CI 89.5% to 99.95%) into an 89.8%-precise auto-flag tier and a review tier of 7.1% of traffic; against the 0.5 default, frauds cleared without human review fell from 12 to 6 of 75 (paired bootstrap 95% CI 2 to 11 fewer)."
  ]
}
